{
  "description": "To reinstate and enhance the historic character of the building, the existing ground floor rear glazed door and windows will be replaced with traditional-style timber-framed French doors incorporating double-glazed toughened glass, flanked by matching timber-framed, double-glazed toughened-glass opening windows.\n\nThe two existing ground floor flat sash windows, one to the front elevation and one to the rear elevation, will be replaced with timber-framed, double-glazed toughened-glass sash windows. The existing bathroom side-hung casement window will also be replaced with a timber-framed, double-glazed toughened-glass fanlight opening window.\n\nThe proposed alterations are intended to complement and preserve the architectural character of the building while incorporating modern glazing to improve thermal performance.",
